    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** (76.88) serving as the anchor of the lineup. Facing Chris Bassitt, **Junior Caminero** benefits from a strong SP skill projection (+19%) and a favorable #3 slot in the order, making him our highest-ceiling asset today. **Yordan Alvarez** (71.66) follows closely behind, backed by an elite xwOBA of 0.464; despite a matchup against George Kirby, **Yordan Alvarez** maintains high efficiency due to his placement in the #2 hole and a positive platoon adjustment. **Caleb Durbin** (64.84) remains a primary objective for stolen base accumulation; his speed remains a prioritized variable, and he draws a favorable matchup against Bubba Chandler, who is prone to allowing base runners and offers an exploitable SP skill metric.\n\nTactical adjustments highlight the importance of matchup context for today\u2019s lineup. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (58.71) is a high-upside play at 3B, bolstered by a +11% SP skill edge against Steven Matz and a high xwOBA (0.388). Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (62.44) is locked into the #1 slot against Liberatore; while his dynamic platoon split as a lefty against a lefty is penalized, his position at the top of the order ensures enough plate appearances to mitigate that risk. **Christian Yelich** (57.80) also represents a significant value-add, as his dynamic platoon advantage (+13%) against Yoshinobu Yamamoto overrides the high caliber of the opposing arm.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Carson Benge** (42.83), who was the first player excluded from the starting nine. While **Carson Benge** possesses a respectable base projection, he faced a negative platoon-on-platoon disadvantage against Andrew Alvarez, which effectively capped his daily efficiency score below our threshold. The benching of **Lars Nootbaar** (36.52) was more straightforward; facing an elite arm in Chris Sale, the risk of a sub-40 efficiency score was too high given the team's cap management strategy. Finally, we note that **Trea Turner** is unavailable due to an off-day, placing increased pressure on **Caleb Durbin** and **Chase Meidroth** to maintain our stolen base production against their respective opponents. Managers should monitor official lineups for **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, and **Kazuma Okamoto**, as any shift downward in their expected batting order could further dampen their already marginal projections.",
